[
  {
    "id": "disksec-world-writable-files",
    "fix": "chmod -R go-w ~/.claude/permission-gate ~/.claude/skills ~/.claude/mods ~/.claude/global-memory ~/.claude/scripts ~/.claude/hooks; chmod 600 ~/.claude/permission-gate/shadow.jsonl ~/.claude/settings.json.bak ~/.claude/settings.json.bak-20260713-153814 ~/.claude/settings.json.bak-20260910-143831 ~/.claude/settings.json.bak-before-shadow-gate-20260922 ~/.claude/settings.json.bak-before-skill-router-20260919-125000 ~/DEV/Football/CFB_Playoff_Benchmarks/.env ~/.config/gws/client_secret.json ~/.config/gws/client_secret.json.bak-2026-06-19; chmod 700 ~/.ssh. Leave out Keychain single-sourcing of PFF/CATAPULT keys (live pipelines), the SSH passphrase, .claude.json.tmp and cli-proxy-api. Those are Eric's.",
    "critic_reason": "Confirmed: permission-gate/*.py and shadow.jsonl are 0666 (the gate hook is executable code), 5 settings.json.bak* files are 0666, CFB .env is 0644, gws client_secret.json and .bak-2026-06-19 are 0644, ~/.ssh is 0755. Home is 0750, so the exposure is group staff. chmod only, owner access is unchanged, and git ignores write bits. Merges settings-hooks-world-writable-hook-and-creds, dev-env-key-duplication (chmod part), disksec-cfb-benchmarks-env-644 and gaps-misc-cred-perms.",
    "original_finding": "Run 'chmod -R go-w ~/.claude/permission-gate ~/.claude/skills ~/.claude/mods ~/.claude/global-memory ~/.claude/scripts ~/.claude/hooks' now. Run the full 'chmod -R go-w ~/.claude' after the _windows-import-archive prune.",
    "evidence": "9,670 world-writable files remain (_windows-import-archive 4719, file-history 2155, context-mode 1333, session-env 1191, skills 61, global-memory 51, mods 25). permission-gate/{rules.py,sanitize.py,shadow_hook.py,shadow.jsonl} are still -rw-rw-rw-. Home is drwxr-x---."
  },
  {
    "id": "disksec-tool-caches",
    "fix": "mv ~/.cache/codex-runtimes/codex-runtime-install-ukjF75 ~/.Trash/. Clear only the download cache: `rm -rf \"$(brew --cache)\"/downloads/*` (not `brew cleanup`). grep -rl token-dashboard ~/DEV ~/.claude/settings.json ~/.claude/scripts and the LaunchAgents. If nothing references it, mv ~/.claude/token-dashboard.db ~/.Trash/. Never touch codex-primary-runtime or the live ~/.memsearch/milvus.db. uv cache prune stays blocked.",
    "critic_reason": "Confirmed: codex-runtime-install-ukjF75 is 1.9G, from Oct 16, absent from config.toml (which uses codex-primary-runtime), and lsof shows nothing open. Homebrew cache is 1.5G. Disk has 96Gi free, so value is low. `brew cleanup` is replaced with a download-cache-only removal, because brew cleanup also uninstalls old kegs that venvs may reference. Merges gaps-codex-runtime-not-leftover and the token-dashboard part of mp-orphan-stores.",
    "original_finding": "Move ~/.cache/codex-runtimes/codex-runtime-install-ukjF75 (1.9G, no process uses it) to ~/.Trash and run `brew cleanup` (Homebrew cache 1.5G). `~/.local/bin/uv cache prune` stays blocked until the browser-use MCP sessions are closed.",
    "evidence": "npm cache is down to 660K (done). ~/.cache/uv is still 23G (known blocked). codex-runtime-install-ukjF75 is still 1.9G and no running process references it. Disk has 96Gi free (78% used)."
  },
  {
    "id": "dev-merged-branches-worktrees-not-cleaned",
    "fix": "Find real paths first (find ~/DEV -maxdepth 3 -type d -name PFF_Data_Project -o -name project-triage -o -name SportScienceResearchRepo -o -name ZoteroInjestion). In each repo run git fetch, then `git branch --merged origin/main` (the rule's form, not plain --merged), check there are no uncommitted changes, and `git branch -d` only the listed branches. Leave the current branch and main alone. Run `git -C ~/DEV/Flint worktree prune`. Skip remote deletes and the FaceComps mock-week-deck folder until the hash-object check passes. Report in one line.",
    "critic_reason": "Covered by Eric's standing post-merge permission (feedback_post-merge-cleanup). Confirmed 10 merged branches in Football/SpeedProfiling, 2 in Football/FaceComps and 3 prunable Flint worktrees. The other 4 repo paths did not resolve in my check. Low value but pre-approved and reversible through the reflog.",
    "original_finding": "Under the standing post-merge permission: git branch -d the merged local branches (SpeedProfiling 10, FaceComps 2, PFF_Data_Project 1, project-triage 1, SportScienceResearchRepo 1, LibraryProject/ZoteroInjestion 1) and git -C ~/DEV/Flint worktree prune; leave remote deletes and the FaceComps .claude/worktrees/mock-week-deck orphan folder until each file passes the hash-object check.",
    "evidence": "Merged local branch counts as listed; Flint has 3 prunable /private/tmp worktrees; mock-week-deck .git points to C:/Users/eric_rash/... and its 222 files are still in cloud-push files0.bin."
  },
  {
    "id": "gaps-desktop-commander-logging",
    "fix": "Set telemetryEnabled false through the desktop-commander set_config_value tool (or a jq edit with backup). chmod 600 ~/.claude-server-commander/tool-history.jsonl ~/.claude-server-commander/claude_tool_call.log.",
    "critic_reason": "Confirmed: telemetryEnabled is True and both logs are mode 644. Setting the flag and chmod change nothing functional. Low value. Plugin removal stays with Eric.",
    "original_finding": "Set telemetryEnabled false in ~/.claude-server-commander/config.json (via set_config_value) and chmod 600 ~/.claude-server-commander/tool-history.jsonl and claude_tool_call.log; leave plugin removal for Eric.",
    "evidence": "config.json today: telemetryEnabled True, allowedDirectories []; both logs still mode 644, last written Sep 13"
  }
]

